  "body": "## What changed\n\nKeep Sodick control-side G41/G42 H offsets and same-path skim passes unsupported, as the issue's decision option permits.\nName the operation when a COMP record requests unsupported compensation.\nSuppress later cuts in that section.\nKeep the refusal across section start and COMP OFF.\nReset it at section end so a later plain section still posts.\nRecord the decision and the requirements for future support.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe document stores no H-register identifiers or values.\nThe wire laws judge generated wire-centre paths and cannot certify an offset chosen separately at the control.\nThe missing compensation hook already caused an engine warning that blocked app output.\nThe script still emitted affected cutting blocks in diagnostic output.\n\n## Tests (pins, mutation results)\n\nPins in `crates/post/tests/sodick_comp.rs`:\n\n- `sodick_control_and_wear_offsets_before_section_refuse_without_cutting`\n- `sodick_control_and_wear_offsets_inside_section_stop_subsequent_cuts`\n- `sodick_comp_cancel_does_not_reenable_a_refused_section`\n- `sodick_comp_request_stops_a_following_arc`\n- `sodick_standalone_comp_off_is_refused_as_an_unsupported_record`\n- `sodick_comp_refusal_resets_for_the_next_plain_section`\n- `sodick_plain_wire_centre_stream_still_posts`\n\nUnchanged code failed six pins and passed the plain-path control.\nThe fixed script passed all seven.\nRestoring the whole old script reproduced six failures.\nRestoring the fix passed all seven again.\nRemoving the section-start check, the hook's `sectionOk = false`, or the section-end reset each failed its targeted pin.\nRestoring each guard passed its pin.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed 28 suites and 212 tests.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\nThe existing app Sodick golden and skim-refusal tests passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\nThe `.nc` and `.cl` diff is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo physical Sodick hardware was exercised.\nH-word formatting, control-side offsets, and same-path skim support remain intentionally unimplemented.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone.\nOpen-PR file queries found no overlap for the three changed files.\nThe branch starts from upstream/main `8719d8b7`.\n\nChangelog: Give unsupported Sodick wire compensation requests an operation-specific refusal and suppress affected cutting blocks.\n\nFixes #1498\n",
